descriptions.job-1ln0t3f:
&lt;p&gt;Square is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Square Partnerships, APAC&lt;/strong&gt; to define and lead the strategic partnerships vision across Australia and Japan. This leader will build and scale partnerships that accelerate Square Seller acquisition, product adoption, ecosystem expansion, and long-term business growth throughout the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partners span referral networks, distributors, financial institutions, technology platforms, service providers, commerce ecosystems, and other strategic partners where there is mutual value through lead generation, co-selling, co-marketing, product enablement, and selective product integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is one of Square&#39;s most senior partnerships leadership roles, operating at the intersection of business development, growth, product, and go-to-market strategy. You will own the APAC partnerships strategy, lead a high-performing regional organization, influence product and commercial direction, and represent Square externally with senior executives across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Australia and leads partnerships across both Australia and Japan. Regular travel throughout APAC, including Japan, and to the United States is expected to build executive relationships, support strategic partners, and collaborate closely with Sales, Account Management, Marketing, Product, Strategy and executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Strategy &amp;amp; Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Define and execute the long-term partnerships strategy for Australia and Japan, aligning investment priorities with Square&#39;s regional growth strategy, product roadmap, and commercial objectives. Identify emerging ecosystem opportunities that strengthen Square&#39;s competitive position and accelerate sustainable business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Partner Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identify, evaluate, negotiate, and scale high-impact partnerships across key industries and ecosystems. Build a diversified portfolio of partners that expands Square&#39;s distribution, enhances our product capabilities, and creates differentiated value for sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Develop trusted relationships with C-level executives and senior decision-makers across strategic partners. Lead complex commercial negotiations and structure partnerships that deliver long-term value for Square, our partners, and our sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Growth &amp;amp; Commercial Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Own measurable partnership outcomes across seller acquisition, pipeline generation, revenue growth, product adoption, ecosystem expansion, and strategic market development. Establish clear business objectives and ensure partnerships deliver meaningful commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership Activation &amp;amp; Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Lead the successful launch and scaling of strategic partnerships through coordinated go-to-market execution, co-selling, co-marketing, product enablement, partner success programs, and selective product integrations. Drive ongoing optimization through executive business reviews and operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Partner closely with Sales, Account Management, Strategy, Marketing, Product, Engineering, Finance, Legal, Operations, Compliance, and regional leadership to prioritize investments, influence product roadmaps, remove execution barriers, and maximize partnership impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Strategy &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Continuously evaluate the regional partnership portfolio, balancing strategic investments with measurable business outcomes. Allocate resources toward the highest-impact opportunities while evolving strategy based on market trends, competitive dynamics, customer needs, and business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Build, lead, and develop a world-class partnerships organization across Australia and Japan. Develop exceptional talent, coach future leaders, establish operating rhythms, and foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, innovation, and customer obsession.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the senior partnerships leader for APAC, representing the region with Square and Block executives. Provide strategic recommendations informed by market insights, competitive intelligence, and partner feedback while influencing global partnerships, product, and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, growth, product partnerships, or related leadership roles, including 8+ years leading senior teams and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of developing and scaling regional or global partnership strategies that drive measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience negotiating complex commercial agreements that drive mutual growth, and managing executive-level strategic relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success influencing senior executives and cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and financial acumen, including experience evaluating partnership investments, structuring business models, and managing portfolio performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing geographically distributed teams while fostering strong collaboration across markets and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product, Engineering and Strategy to influence product strategy, integrations, and ecosystem development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS, fintech, payments, commerce, or financial services experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of both the Australian business landscape required; experience working across Japan or broader APAC markets strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in Australia (Sydney preferred), with the ability to travel regularly throughout APAC, including Japan, and to the United States to support executive engagement, strategic partner development, and cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic, commercial mindset with the ability to translate long-term vision into measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive presence and relationship-building skills, with a track record of influencing senior leaders both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and the ability to structure partnerships that create sustainable value for all parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to turn a strong commercial deal into a growth machine with clear KPIs, enablement, operational rigor, and optimization levers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding leadership skills with experience building high-performing, globally distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in ambiguity, prioritize effectively, and lead through change in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and storytelling skills, capable of influencing audiences ranging from partner executives to Square&#39;s senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for building enduring partnerships that create meaningful value for sellers and strengthen Square&#39;s position across the APAC ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to define the future of Square&#39;s partnerships strategy across two of our most important international markets. As the senior partnerships leader for APAC, you will shape how Square expands its ecosystem, accelerates growth, influences product strategy, and delivers greater value to sellers through world-class strategic partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a global Partnerships organization that works across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, and executive leadership to build relationships that create lasting competitive advantage for Square and Block.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may submit up to 9 active applications within a 60-day period. Reapplications to the same role are accepted 90 days after a previous application has been reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We may use automated AI tools to evaluate job applications for efficiency and consistency. These tools comply with local regulations, including bias audits, and we handle all personal data in accordance with state and local privacy laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact us &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.block.xyz/privacyportal/form&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with hiring practice or data usage questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Every benefit we offer is designed with one goal: empowering you to do the best work of your career while building the life you want. Remote work, medical insurance, flexible time off, retirement savings plans, and modern family planning are just some of our offering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://block.xyz/employee-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/benefits.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Check out our other benefits at Block.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Block, Inc. (NYSE: XYZ) builds technology to increase access to the global economy. Each of our brands unlocks different aspects of the economy for more people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Square&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;makes commerce and financial services accessible to sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Cash App&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the easy way to spend, send, and store money.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Afterpay&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is transforming the way customers manage their spending over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;TIDAL&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music platform that empowers artists to thrive as entrepreneurs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Bitkey&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a simple self-custody wallet built for bitcoin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Proto&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a suite of bitcoin mining products and services. Together, we’re helping build a financial system that is open to everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/en/legal/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-164oqyz:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a mid-level Software Engineer with a strong backend focus to join our Fiat Payment Products team. You will build and operate the systems behind our fiat and stablecoin payment rails, including our Public API that powers deposits, payouts, swaps, and settlement for merchants like crypto exchanges, PSPs, and fintech platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is primarily backend. You will work closely with product managers, fellow engineers, and integration support to deliver on the roadmap and keep production systems reliable as merchant traffic scales. We value technical proficiency, clear communication, ownership, and the ability to work independently. Experience with financial systems or crypto is a plus, and any frontend experience is welcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver backend features across our fiat and stablecoin payment flows and Public API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers to shape requirements and deliver against the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested, maintainable code and apply engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure system availability and reliability through robust monitoring, stress testing, and maintenance as merchant traffic scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architecture decisions, data-driven tradeoffs, and the design of scalable, secure systems for financial transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, backlog grooming, and sprint planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support merchant integrations and L2 investigation alongside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with frontend engineers to integrate backend services smoothly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of backend engineering experience, proficient in a language such as Ruby on Rails, Golang or other related backend technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and relational database design (MySQL or PostgreSQL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of RESTful APIs and microservices architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grounding in system design principles and building for scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with CI/CD concepts and version control (Git).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good written and spoken English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI assisted engineering workflows is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial systems, payments, or fintech infrastructure is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with crypto, stablecoins, or blockchain is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Agile delivery is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend familiarity (React, TypeScript, or JavaScript) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0avmxaj:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that we are unable to consider applications from candidates based in France, Italy, or Germany for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Money is moving onto the internet, and the shift has a name: &lt;strong&gt;Open Money. &lt;/strong&gt;This is money that is open, portable, agentic, and owned by you. MetaMask spent the last ten years building it; with 100M+ downloads, users in ~190 countries, and trillions in cumulative transaction volume, it&#39;s the most trusted self-custodial financial platform on the internet. Now we&#39;re building the operating system for your money: one place to hold, move, grow, and use anything you own.&amp;nbsp; Join a remote-first, global team rebuilding how money works: a problem that touches everyone, every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About PODS Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People and Talent support the members of our Consensys community. We strive to be the destination employer of choice for our ecosystem. That goal is embedded in all the work we do to attract, retain and support our incredible talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PODS — People Operations, Data &amp;amp; Systems — is the infrastructure layer behind everything our People team does — the systems, data, and operational processes that make it possible to hire, pay, onboard, develop, and support people at scale. When this function works well, it&#39;s invisible. When it doesn&#39;t, everyone notices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone to take ownership of our core People systems. In this role, you will be the primary subject matter expert on ADP Workforce Now and the broader HR technology ecosystem, the person Finance calls when People data doesn&#39;t match, the person Legal calls when they need audit evidence, and the person the People &amp;amp; Talent team relies on for system builds, enhancements, and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HRIS administration and system integrity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are the technical owner of ADP Workforce Now and the PODS technology ecosystem. System health, configuration, data integrity, and day-to-day administration are yours — not tasks you contribute to, but outcomes you own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform ownership — &lt;/strong&gt;Manage day-to-day ADP WFN configuration, security roles, workflows, custom fields, and system health. You know where everything is, why it&#39;s set up the way it is, and what breaks if it changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business process design — &lt;/strong&gt;Take business needs from requirements through configuration, testing, and post-launch validation — end to end, without handing off. When a stakeholder brings you a problem, you translate it into a working system solution and own it through to adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product releases — &lt;/strong&gt;Own configuration, testing, and rollout of new ADP product releases and system enhancements. Proactively flag opportunities to simplify or automate existing processes before problems surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration management — &lt;/strong&gt;Own all system integrations across payroll entities, benefits carriers, finance tools, and core HR platforms — both automated API connections and manual data flows. Monitor, troubleshoot, and escalate when things break.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and access — &lt;/strong&gt;Manage role-based access across HR systems, enforce least-privilege standards, and maintain SOX-ready access review evidence on a defined cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor management — &lt;/strong&gt;Own day-to-day vendor relationships across the stack — performance accountability, escalation paths, SLA tracking, and contract awareness. Not just ticket submission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical project ownership and process automation&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You lead technical workstreams from intake through completion — representing the People Operations perspective on systems, data, and integration projects across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical project ownership — &lt;/strong&gt;Own HR systems and data projects end to end — scoping, configuration, testing, rollout, and documentation. You represent PODS interests in cross-functional projects and ensure the People Operations perspective is built into technical decisions, not bolted on afterward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process automation — &lt;/strong&gt;Systematically replace manual, error-prone workflows with automated processes. Use AI-assisted tools to rapidly prototype and build People Operations automations — turning process ideas into working solutions on fast, business-critical timelines. Measure the reduction in manual effort and error rates over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOX and compliance — &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain documented controls, gather and organize audit evidence, and partner with Legal and Finance to ensure People systems meet compliance requirements at every stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change management — &lt;/strong&gt;Test before deploying. Document after deploying. Communicate to stakeholders before either. Every system change has a testing plan, a rollout plan, and a runbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data management and stakeholder enablement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are the check-and-balance for People data across the organization — and the person who makes that data accessible and understandable to the people who depend on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data governance — &lt;/strong&gt;Establish and maintain data definitions, quality standards, field ownership, and retention policies. When two stakeholders get different answers to the same question, you are the reason that stops happening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting and analysis — &lt;/strong&gt;Prepare, review, and analyze People data and reports. Build custom reports and executive-facing dashboards in ADP and connected tools. Translate outputs into clear, actionable information for Finance, FP&amp;amp;A, Legal, and People leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audits — &lt;/strong&gt;Run recurring data audits, maintain audit logs, and ensure evidence is organized and retrievable. Catch discrepancies before they reach stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation and training — &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain up-to-date process documentation and deliver training materials for new system enhancements. Build genuine self-service capability in the HR team — reducing the ad hoc support load over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational support&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You provide timely, effective support for daily system needs and cyclical operations — and you use patterns in that support to build lasting fixes rather than repeat the same interventions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee and manager support — &lt;/strong&gt;Provide responsive support for system questions, access issues, and ad hoc requests. Identify recurring patterns and build runbooks or automations to address root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cyclical operations — &lt;/strong&gt;Own the systems side of open enrollment, compensation cycles, re-orgs, payroll close, and year-end processes. These run on a schedule — they need to run without heroics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor relationships — &lt;/strong&gt;Hold vendors accountable to SLAs, manage escalations above the support queue, and keep contract renewal dates on the radar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Would be great if you brought this to the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive experience in HR systems administration, HRIS configuration, or HR technology operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of business process design end to end — you&#39;ve taken requirements from a stakeholder conversation through configuration, testing, launch, and post-launch validation without handing off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate ambiguous business needs into working system solutions — you ask the right questions, design the right solution, and build it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with process automation and AI-assisted tooling — you&#39;ve used modern tools to prototype and build automations that eliminated meaningful manual effort, and you can point to the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data management instincts — you&#39;ve built custom reports, run data audits, caught data quality issues before they became business problems, and you understand what governance actually means in practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOX or audit compliance experience — you understand what controls mean, what evidence looks like, and what an auditor will ask for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management capability — you&#39;ve managed a high volume of requests and shifting priorities without losing track of what matters most, and you communicate status without being asked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual curiosity and sound judgment — you ask why something works the way it does, and you know when to move fast and when to slow down and think&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;A bias for action paired with resilience in ambiguity — you&#39;ve operated in fast-moving environments where requirements changed mid-project and you didn&#39;t wait for perfect information to make progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Don&#39;t meet all the requirements? Don&#39;t sweat it. We’re passionate about building a diverse team of humans and as such, if you think you&#39;ve got what it takes for our chaotic-but-fun, remote-friendly, start-up environment—apply anyway, detailing your relevant transferable skills in your cover letter. While we have a pretty good idea of what we need, we&#39;re ready for you to challenge our thinking on who needs to be in this role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #e03e2d;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;It is a requirement of employment in this position that applicants will be required to submit to background checks including but not limited to employment, education and criminal record checks. Further details will be provided to applicants that successfully meet the criteria for the position as determined by the company in its sole discretion. By submitting an application for employment, you are acknowledging and consenting to this requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The salary range listed for this role applies to US-based candidates only. Compensation for candidates based outside the US (including Canada, EMEA, and LATAM) will be determined based on location, experience, and skills during the interview process, and may differ from the listed US range.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US pay range (not including bonus, equity or other benefits)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$122,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$183,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;In the rapidly evolving Web3 space, we believe that everyone is a builder. This expansive paradigm requires a range of backgrounds, talents, skills, and experiences to influence and shape the future. At MetaMask, this diversity fuels our ability to shift control and redefine the realm of possibility. We are committed to ensuring that our technology empowers people and communities through decentralized technologies. We welcome the range of perspectives and differences and celebrate them. We&#39;re excited to see how your unique skills as a builder can contribute to our vision, drive innovation, and help us shape a more inclusive Web3.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;MetaMask is an equal opportunity employer. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, religion, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, marital status, family status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;MetaMask is aware of fraudulent recruitment practices and we encourage all applicants to review our best practices to protect yourself, which can be found on our page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;MetaMask may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of our recruitment process, such as reviewing applications, screening resumes, or conducting initial candidate assessments. These tools are designed to assist our recruiting team and improve efficiency — they do not replace human judgment. A human recruiter or hiring manager reviews every candidate, and all final hiring decisions are made by people, not AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is a requirement of employment in this position that applicants may be required to submit to background and identity verification checks, including but not limited to employment, education, criminal record checks, and other such checks as determined necessary by the company.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

